<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Timestamp on Sebastian Hoß</title><link>https://seb.xn--ho-hia.de/tags/timestamp/</link><description>Recent content in Timestamp on Sebastian Hoß</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 06 Jan 2023 15:27:21 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://seb.xn--ho-hia.de/tags/timestamp/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Create Timestamp with GitHub Actions</title><link>https://seb.xn--ho-hia.de/posts/github-actions-create-timestamp/</link><pubDate>Thu, 11 Jun 2020 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://seb.xn--ho-hia.de/posts/github-actions-create-timestamp/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;In case you are into &lt;a href="https://calver.org/"&gt;calver&lt;/a&gt; or have another reason to create a timestamp with &lt;a href="https://github.com/features/actions"&gt;GitHub Actions&lt;/a&gt;, do the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-yaml" data-lang="yaml"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;&amp;lt;PIPELINE&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;jobs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;runs-on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;&amp;lt;RUN_ON&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;steps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;- &lt;span class="nt"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;Create release version&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;&amp;lt;ID&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;echo &amp;#34;::set-output name=&amp;lt;NAME&amp;gt;::$(date +&amp;#39;%Y.%m.%d-%H%M%S&amp;#39;)&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;PIPELINE&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;: The name of your pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;RUN_ON&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;: The runner to use, see GitHub&amp;rsquo;s own &lt;a href="https://help.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflow-syntax-for-github-actions#jobsjob_idruns-on"&gt;documentation&lt;/a&gt; for possible values.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;ID&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;: The unique ID of the timestamp step.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;NAME&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;: The name of the created timestamp.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The special syntax &lt;code&gt;::set-output name=&amp;lt;NAME&amp;gt;::&lt;/code&gt; declares that the output of the command (&lt;code&gt;echo&lt;/code&gt;) should be saved in a variable called &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;NAME&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. Together with the &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;ID&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; of the pipeline step, this value can be referenced with the expression &lt;code&gt;${{ steps.&amp;lt;ID&amp;gt;.outputs.&amp;lt;NAME&amp;gt; }}&lt;/code&gt; in the following steps of your pipeline.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>